# scope

this document supports **vite‑based** react projects integrating `@dytesdk/react‑web‑core` and `@dytesdk/react‑ui‑kit` (ui kit v1.x). other frameworks are out of scope.

---

# prerequisites

```bash
npm install --save-exact @dytesdk/react-web-core @dytesdk/react-ui-kit
npm install --save-dev vite @vitejs/plugin-react typescript
```

*minimum node ≥ 18.14.0*

---

# environment variables (vite only exposes `VITE_*`)

```env
VITE_DYTE_AUTH_TOKEN="${PARTICIPANT_AUTH_TOKEN}"
VITE_DYTE_BASE_URL="https://api.cluster.dyte.in/v2" # optional
```

---

# vite configuration

```ts title="vite.config.ts"
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  define: {
    global: 'window', // required by react‑web‑core
  },
  optimizeDeps: {
    include: ['@dytesdk/react-web-core', '@dytesdk/react-ui-kit'],
  },
});
```

---

# minimal implementation blueprint

```tsx title="App.tsx"
import { useEffect } from 'react';
import { DyteProvider, useDyteClient } from '@dytesdk/react-web-core';
import { DyteMeeting } from '@dytesdk/react-ui-kit';

export default function App() {
  const [meeting, initMeeting] = useDyteClient();

  useEffect(() => {
    initMeeting({
      authToken: import.meta.env.VITE_DYTE_AUTH_TOKEN,
      defaults: { audio: false, video: false },
    });
  }, []);

  if (!meeting) return null; // sdk initialising

  return (
    <DyteProvider value={meeting}>
      <DyteMeeting meeting={meeting} mode="fill" showSetupScreen={false} />
    </DyteProvider>
  );
}
```

## server‑side token issuance

call **create meeting → add participant** rest endpoints to retrieve `authToken`. tokens expire per ttl (default 24 h). regenerate on `MeetingEnded` or http 401.

